          "#text": "Formic acid is an industrially important chemical frequently used as a preservative and antibacterial agent in livestock feed, among other applications. It's involved in various production processes such as leather processing, dyeing, fabric treatment, and rubber manufacturing. This product is commonly available as a consumable in chemical formulations or as a reagent in laboratories, typically 'to consumer' or 'at plant', meeting relevant quality and safety standards.",
